1. DEFINITIONS
   1.1 "Software" means the CanvasXpress JavaScript distribution (the canvasxpress
       browser bundle and files distributed with it), in source or compiled form.
   1.2 "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
       License.
   1.3 "The Mark" means the CanvasXpress attribution notice the Software renders
       on its output (the on-canvas watermark and any equivalent attribution the
       Software emits).
   1.4 "Commercial License" means a separate paid agreement from CanvasXpress that
       grants the right to suppress the Mark.
   1.5 "License Key" means a credential issued by CanvasXpress (including any
       domain-bound token) that, when validly present, suppresses the Mark.

2. GRANT OF RIGHTS (COMMUNITY TIER)
   Subject to Section 3, CanvasXpress grants You a worldwide, royalty-free,
   non-exclusive license to use, copy, modify, and distribute the Software and
   works built with it, for any purpose including commercial purposes, at no
   charge.

3. CONDITIONS
   3.1 Attribution. The Mark the Software renders must remain visible and
       unaltered in all output the Software produces. You must not remove, hide,
       obscure, resize into illegibility, reposition off-canvas, recolor to match
       the background, disable, or otherwise defeat the Mark by any means -- in the
       source, at build time, or at runtime -- unless You hold a current Commercial
       License.

   3.2 No circumvention (technological protection measure). The License Key check
       and the Mark-rendering code together constitute a technological protection
       measure ("TPM") that controls access to the un-marked form of the Software.
       You must not disable, bypass, circumvent, remove, spoof, decrypt,
       descramble, or otherwise defeat that TPM, and you must not manufacture,
       distribute, or make available any product, code, service, or information
       primarily designed or produced to do so, whether performed in the source, at
       build time, or at runtime. Forging, sharing, or reusing a License Key beyond
       its issued scope is a material breach and an act of circumvention. The
       parties acknowledge that this TPM is protected by anti-circumvention law,
       including 17 U.S.C. Section 1201 (U.S. DMCA) and Article 6 of Directive
       2001/29/EC (EU) and their equivalents, and that circumvention gives rise to
       statutory remedies in addition to any remedy for breach of this License.

   3.3 No reverse engineering (with interoperability carve-out). You must not
       reverse assemble, reverse compile, or reverse engineer the Software, or
       cause a third party to do so, for the purpose of defeating the TPM in
       Section 3.2 or removing the Mark. This Section 3.3 does not prohibit, and
       nothing in this License restricts, reverse engineering that is permitted by
       applicable non-waivable law -- including decompilation for interoperability
       under Article 6 of Directive 2009/24/EC (EU Software Directive) -- to the
       extent such reverse engineering is not used to circumvent the TPM or remove
       the Mark.

   3.4 Notices. You must retain this License text, the copyright notice, and the
       disclaimer in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

   3.5 No misrepresentation. You must not remove or alter the origin of the
       Software or represent it as your own original work, and you must not use the
       CanvasXpress name or marks to endorse products derived from the Software
       without permission.

4. COMMERCIAL LICENSE (MARK SUPPRESSION)
   The right to suppress the Mark is not granted by this License and is available
   only under a Commercial License. A valid License Key issued under a Commercial
   License suppresses the Mark automatically; this is a permitted exercise of that
   License and is not a breach of Section 3. Commercial Licenses may be scoped (per
   developer, per domain, per term) as stated at purchase.

5. TERMINATION
   If You breach Section 3, the rights granted under Section 2 terminate
   automatically. They are reinstated prospectively if You cure the breach within
   30 days of becoming aware of it. A Commercial License, if held, governs its own
   termination.

